rectangle "nyx\n<size:16>[Software System]</size>" <<Boundary-bnl4>> {
  rectangle "app\n<size:16>[Container: Rust, eframe/egui]</size>" <<Boundary-YXBw>> {
    rectangle "==Viewport\n<size:16>[Component: Rust modules]</size>\n\nThe 2D/3D viewport: camera, drawing of meshes and result fields, picking, colour maps, the colour slots of regions (solid, hatched, grey) with their number chips and legend, and what is kept between frames." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQ=>> as nyx.app.Viewport
    rectangle "==Look and widgets\n<size:16>[Component: Rust modules]</size>\n\nThe nyx look (the colour tokens as data, fonts, egui visuals, light and dark, contrast) and the small brand widgets (cards, chips, buttons, glyphs, sparklines, sheets), and how numbers and counts are written." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQ=>> as nyx.app.Lookandwidgets
    rectangle "==Scripts and batch\n<size:16>[Component: Rust modules]</size>\n\nRuns without a person at the window: scripted runs with screenshots (--script), batch runs for clusters, command lists (nyx check, nyx run) and the command reference (nyx api), and the optional user Python script." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQ=>> as nyx.app.Scriptsandbatch
    rectangle "==Window\n<size:16>[Component: Rust modules]</size>\n\nThe application object around one Engine: window layout, the run-time state (mesh on show, result on show, plot settings) and the frame update loop." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQ=>> as nyx.app.Window
    rectangle "==Shell and dashboard\n<size:16>[Component: Rust modules]</size>\n\nThe tab bar, the native menu and the table of actions it shares with the palette, the dashboard of workflows with live status, the busy chip and queue popover read from the engine queue, the workflow view (concept, build with its Sweep section, analysis), the sheets (new, search, versions, share, settings) and the example starting points." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQ=>> as nyx.app.Shellanddashboard
    rectangle "==Inspector tabs\n<size:16>[Component: Rust modules]</size>\n\nThe tabs beside the viewport: geometry editor, materials, physics, study, results, analysis. Forms are drawn from the physics descriptors; the geometry editor generates one form per feature kind." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQ=>> as nyx.app.Inspectortabs
  }

  rectangle "==nyx-script\n<size:16>[Container: Rust library and worker binary]</size>\n\nScripts, a third front-end of the engine: Python-syntax text (*.nys) run by Monty in a worker process; each nyx.<command>(...) is one Engine::call. Limits, no ambient access, the engine's path guard." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb250YWluZXIsRXhlY3V0YWJsZQ==>> as nyx.nyxscript
  rectangle "==nyx-connect\n<size:16>[Container: Rust library and binary]</size>\n\nFinds Claude Code and Claude Desktop installs and registers nyx-mcp with them; the Connect menu and its command-line twin." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb250YWluZXIsRXhlY3V0YWJsZQ==>> as nyx.nyxconnect
  component "==nyx-engine\n<size:16>[Container: Rust library]</size>\n\nThe Engine: one project, the mesh built for it, the latest result of each physics, the jobs that produce them, and the binding to a workflow. Every action is a named command with a JSON Schema." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb250YWluZXIsTGlicmFyeQ==>> as nyx.nyxengine
}

